  "notes": [
    "Actual signing and verification operations move by operation; Python and Go symbol references, a JVM class name, and a diagnostic string move to their evidenced subjects.",
    "The Go key/signing composite description no longer claims observed signing or data flow. No directory-level YAML consumers reference the legacy signature leaf.",
    "The hexadecimal DigestInfo prefix is an encoded constant; its presence does not itself establish signing or verification.",
    "A decoded alert is an encoded-text observation, freeing a call-syntax slot for signatureImport without claiming an operation from an unqualified helper name.",
    "The Ed25519 domain separator indicates the named primitive, without establishing a signing or verification operation.",
    "Removed the unreferenced decode-and-minisign composite and its benign-context exception: subprocess text, a filename fragment, or the shared untrusted-comment header near a decode does not establish benign verification. This intentionally restores the encoded shell subprocess detection for those combinations absent other exceptions.",
    "A browser executable-name observation moved to the browser path category, allowing the SignedXml name to enter the existing binary symbol token category without changing the directory cap."
  ],
